<title>GERMANY: Buba's Issing says capital mkt rates could fall.</title>
<headline>Buba's Issing says capital mkt rates could fall.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank chief economist Otmar Issing said on Monday that capital market rates could still go lower.</p>
<p>&quot;If one has declared inflation to be dead and one were not to expect inflation to be resurrected, then one could possibly see lower nominal rates (at the long-end of the market),&quot; Issing told reporters at a bankers' forum.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
